      "owner": "#143",
      "ruled": "2026-07-28",
      "why": "HELD OUT by user ruling 2026-07-28 during #177's grill: this frame is the targeting equation's to answer, not #177's. The correction is valid -- a Crushing Hammer spent on the one Energy attached to a body we are about to knock out is a wasted resource -- and that is a DENY-valuation question, which #143 (Opponent-target unification: one marginal decides snipe/gust/deny) owns. #177 changes KO affordability and touches none of it.\n\nMEASURED, so the owner does not have to re-derive it. The correct option NEVER MOVED: option 0 scores 2207.50 both at the pinned baseline (81eac82) and on current main. Nothing regressed about the human's pick. Pre-change the frame passed only under the LENIENT shared-max rule -- correct_is_unique_top was already False with a FIVE-WAY tie at 2207.50 (options 0,1,2,3,5), because every one of them ends the turn with the same Nebula Beam OHKO and the leaf evaluates the end-of-turn board. Ties break by option order, so the leaf's real pick was index 0 both before and after; the OK verdict was a metric artifact of the tie, not a discrimination success.\n\nWhat flipped it is a SIBLING climbing, not the pick falling: option 6 (Retreat) went 144.50 -> 2231.80 (+2087.30), above the tie and into the KO band, collapsing top_tie 5 -> 1 and taking correct_rank 1 -> 2. This is ADR-0072 finding 1 exactly ('tie-reduction is not a merit metric -- here it is anti-correlated'; the frames that broke were the ones whose ties collapsed).\n\nThe retreat climb is DETERMINISTIC, not #160's RNG noise: re-scored on three independent process runs (2026-07-28), option 6 returned 2231.80 every time, correct_rank 2, top_tie 1. So it is attributable to a merged change, not a stream artifact -- the candidates are #178's 90f7185 (the develop rung may not rank on an RNG-sampled end board) and a777bd7 (a win confirmed off a shuffled deck is undetermined, not True), both of which landed between the baseline pin and 9a0a8ec and both of which touch how a retreat line's rollout is valued. A retreat scoring ABOVE an available, unstoppable 2-prize OHKO is worth the owner's attention on its own merits."
